From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: setup's Full experience, for every account

Dresden, 2026-10-23: the two ways to start are Full experience and Minimal.

- Full experience (preselected): DuckDuckGo for the browser and the
  launcher; Proton's apps installed as web apps (Mail, Calendar, Drive,
  Docs, Pass, Lumo), no longer a bookmarks folder; and a set of free,
  open-source apps (nickel-flatpak-defaults installs them). The web apps
  are Chrome's preinstalled web apps (configs in
  /usr/share/chromium/extensions/web_apps), gated on
  "NickelFullExperience", which IsPreinstalledAppInstallFeatureEnabled()
  answers from the device's choice: it is in local state before the first
  account exists, so the first sync of a new account already has it, and
  Chrome's usual retries, and a user's uninstall being remembered, apply.
- Minimal: the launcher searches only the device; nothing else is set up.

The choice is the device's now, kept in local state rather than cleared
after the first account: every account takes it at its first sign-in.
Choices stored by earlier builds ("default", "privacy") count as Full.

